From: Kali NetHunter rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rhodep: add the flash LED as a torch

The rear camera flash is a plain GPIO on this board. The vendor declares
it as flash-type = <CAM_FLASH_TYPE_GPIO> with gpios = <&tlmm 49 0>, not
through an i2c LED controller, so in mainline terms it is a gpio-led and
nothing more.

Confirmed before writing the node: tlmm 49 was free and unclaimed,
driving it with gpioset blinks the rear LED, and the pin shows as
"GPIO 500000.pinctrl" in pinmux-pins while held.

Exposed as LED_FUNCTION_TORCH rather than as a camera flash on purpose.
A strobe synchronised to an exposure wants the v4l2-flash class and a
camera that captures, and neither exists on this port yet; a flashlight
only has to turn on and stay on. There is a second LED, led_flash_macro
at cell-index 2 in the vendor tree, which is not wired up here.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/interconnect/qcom,rpm-icc.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/interconnect/qcom,sm6375.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/power/qcom-rpmpd.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/qcom,dsi-phy-28nm.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/clock/qcom,sm6375-dispcc.h>
@@ -287,6 +288,29 @@
 		regulator-boot-on;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The rear camera flash. The vendor drives it as a plain GPIO --
+	 * flash-type = <CAM_FLASH_TYPE_GPIO> on tlmm 49 -- rather than through
+	 * an i2c LED controller, so in mainline terms it is a gpio-led and
+	 * nothing more. Confirmed on the device before this node existed:
+	 * tlmm 49 was unclaimed, and driving it blinks the LED.
+	 *
+	 * Exposed as a torch rather than a camera flash on purpose. A strobe
+	 * synchronised to an exposure needs the v4l2-flash class and a camera
+	 * that captures, and neither exists here yet; a flashlight only needs
+	 * to turn on and stay on.
+	 */
+	leds {
+		compatible = "gpio-leds";
+
+		led-torch {
+			gpios = <&tlmm 49 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+			function = LED_FUNCTION_TORCH;
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+			default-state = "off";
+		};
+	};
+
 	vibrator {
 		compatible = "gpio-vibrator";
 		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 100 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
